menu "CYB3RGUN camera bench"

config CGCAM_CLOCK_HZ
    int "SPI clock in Hz"
    range 100000 14000000
    default 1000000
    help
        The part does 14 MHz on a board, but its pins drive 4 mA into a
        specified 100 pF, so flying wires get 1 to 2 MHz. concept.md
        section 5.

config CGCAM_FPS
    int "Frames per second the bench reads at"
    range 1 200
    default 50
    help
        S01-B01 task 5 asks for 50. The part itself does up to 200.

config CGCAM_PRINT_HZ
    int "Lines per second on the serial port"
    range 1 50
    default 2
    help
        The frame loop runs at the full rate so the timing is real. Printing
        every frame at 50 fps would make the port the bottleneck rather than
        the sensor, so only some frames are printed.

endmenu
